From 375b307b6d5de828b3c74510e7a516fd7f66b948 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ken5998 <46025606+Ken5998@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:00:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] feat(input): xinput over sdl2 game controllers on linux

The POSIX input backend was a separate SDL2 path without the keyboard
pad, RECOMP_KEYMAP, RECOMP_PADMAP, the menu pointer or hotplug. Linux now
runs the same code as Windows over xinput_sdl.c, which implements the
XInput calls with SDL2 game controllers (hotplug, packet numbers that
move only on change, held rumble). The keymap regression runs on Linux.
